<span>│</span>
<span>├── index.html</span>
<span>└── couple.jpg</span></span></code></div></div></div><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto"><strong class="font-semibold"><span>Note:</span></strong><span> If your picture is a PNG file, rename the reference in the code to </span><span data-markdown-copy="inline-code" class="InlineCode-Cddi3Y InlineMarkdownIsolate-QWDV4W" dir="ltr">couple.png</span><span> instead.</span></p><h2 class="Heading-Ro3lZr" dir="auto"><span>Step 3: Watch your animation! 🌸</span></h2><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto"><span>When you open the page, you'll see:</span></p><ul class="List-kOVW5V UnorderedList-nqKD7g" dir="auto"><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg"><span>Naruto and Hinata's picture.</span></li><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg"><span>Cherry blossoms falling across the screen.</span></li><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg"><span>Hearts floating upward.</span></li><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg"><span>A pink animated background.</span></li><li class="ListItem-ncLgmg"><span>A button that creates a burst of hearts.</span></li></ul><h3 class="Heading-Ro3lZr" dir="auto"><span>💗 Maggie, one question!</span></h3><p class="Paragraph-kKnbIo" dir="auto"><span>Would you like me to help you make this into a </span><strong class="font-semibold"><span>real MP4 animated video that you can save to your phone and share on Instagram or WhatsApp</span></strong><span>, rather than just an animation running in a browser? 🎬</span></p></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="mt-1.5 flex turn-action-controls min-h-5 min-w-0 max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-wrap items-center justify-start gap-0.5 browser:-ms-0.5 browser:mt-3 electron:-translate-x-1 extension:-translate-x-1.5 [&amp;_button]:focus-visible:ring-2 [&amp;_button]:focus-visible:ring-ring [&amp;_button]:focus-visible:ring-offset-0 [--side-tooltip:bottom]"><div class="flex min-h-5 min-w-0 flex-wrap items-center gap-0.5 browser:gap-0"><span data-state="closed" class="contents"><button type="button" class="no-drag cursor-interaction items-center selec